  "body": "An operator ran `bullet tui` and reported it as *\"dark red against black \u2026 really bad\"*, and that it was *\"NOT obvious what to do\"*. Both are real defects with a single first run behind them.\n\n**Colour.** `tui.rs` chose colour on `NO_COLOR` alone and then emitted 24-bit RGB unconditionally. On a terminal that does not advertise truecolor \u2014 a plain `screen.xterm-256color` with `COLORTERM` unset, the common case under screen and tmux \u2014 the navy ground `Rgb(8,16,31)` quantises to black and the amber chrome `Rgb(255,196,77)` lands on a muddy dark red. That is precisely the reported symptom.\n\nThis adds a `Palette` with three representations and picks one from the terminal's own advertisement: truecolor when `COLORTERM` says so, otherwise indexed ANSI with the ground left to the terminal so the console sits in the operator's theme rather than fighting it with a near-black it cannot reproduce. `NO_COLOR` still wins and still paints every cell `Reset`.\n\n**Guidance.** The bottom bar replaced the key hints with the error text, so the single line naming `Ctrl+K`, `Tab`, `j/k` and `?` vanished exactly when a confused operator needed it \u2014 on a first run with no daemon, the screen was an error, empty panes, and no hints at all. The error now renders above the hints instead of in place of them.\n\nVerified: `operator_tui` 4/4 pass, `bullet` unit tests 64/64 pass including the assertion that `NO_COLOR` leaves every cell `Reset`, `cargo fmt --all --check` clean.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
